invariant: INV-46
file: src/mlkem.c
catches: test/mlkem-builds.sh
reason: mlkem.c's reduction calls mlkem_poly.c's loop in a host object, so
  every session runs it one coefficient at a time. Nothing else objects:
  the loop computes the same coefficients, and only the time is wrong.
  The script compiles mlkem.c as a host object does and requires it to
  call mlk_vector_reduce and not mlk_poly_reduce.

--- old
#ifdef CH_CPU_RUNTIME
    mlk_vector_reduce(p);
#else
    mlk_poly_reduce(p);
--- new
#ifdef CH_CPU_RUNTIME
    mlk_poly_reduce(p);
#else
    mlk_poly_reduce(p);
